<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/tags>
    a gmeow:Slice ;
    rdfs:label "tags"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The tags slice of the GMEOW ontology (core tier): GMEOW Tags Module. Anatomy, dependencies, and consumer are declared in this manifest; the manifest is the sole source of slice identity and tier."@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/tags> ;
    dcterms:title "GMEOW Tags Module"@x-gmeow-english ;
    dcterms:creator "Blackcat Informatics® Inc." ;
    gmeow:sliceTier gmeow:tierCore ;
    gmeow:sliceProfile "memory" ;
    gmeow:sliceDependsOn
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/kernel> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/temporal> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/names> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/provenance> ;
    gmeow:sliceConsumer "The grounded-agent-memory engine (an agent's informal labels over remembered claims ride the same suppression-not-erasure contract as every Principle 14 memory claim), the images and software extensions (dual extension use is what forced the slice core), and the docs/SLICE_GUIDE.md worked instance — this slice is the guide's living example of the competency-first authoring loop, so its competency cells, contested-tagging scene, and honest-rung mappings are load-bearing teaching surfaces, not just tests."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:sliceQualityTier gmeow:tierRegistered .
